{
  "id": "Compound::DB08808 - Gene::155",
  "verbalization": "Bupranolol is implicated in the interaction with Adrb3 through a series of molecular and functional pathways. The evidence suggests that Bupranolol binds to Adrb2, a beta-adrenergic receptor subunit, which in turn participates in multiple functional activities, including Norepinephrine Binding and Epinephrine Binding. These activities are ultimately linked to Adrb3, indicating a potential functional cascade where Bupranolol influences the activity of Adrb3 via Adrb2. The overlapping participation of Adrb2 in different binding processes highlights a possible mechanism by which Bupranolol modulates receptor activity, potentially through a shared functional pathway. The integration of these pathways underscores the role of Adrb2 as a critical mediator in the relationship between Bupranolol and Adrb3, emphasizing the importance of receptor subunit interactions in drug-target mechanisms.",
